  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">223114_Start Fund 846 Honduras Dengue</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project aims to contribute to the emergency response to the dengue epidemic in Honduras the Department of Cort&amp;#233;s and the Central District of Francisco Moraz&amp;#225;n and benefit 42,128 people (11,386 families) with response and prevention actions to confront the outbreak of the dengue-transmitting mosquito. This project is designed to fill gaps in the existing response to an ongoing crisis but also has elements of anticipatory action to mitigate and prevent a possible anticipated spike by preventing ongoing transmission of diseases, and reducing the caseload - thereby reducing morbidity and mortality - which would overwhelm existing capacity and lead to a significant deterioration of the situation.</narrative>
  </description>
